doc:sch-1-sec-6c-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6C(3) Organisations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) In this Act: State or Territory authority means:  (a) a State or Territory Minister; or  (b) a Department of State of a State or Territory; or  (c) a body (whether incorporated or not), or a tribunal, established or appointed for a public purpose by or under a law of a State or Territory, other than:  (i) an incorporated company, society or association; or  (ii) an association of employers or employees that is registered or recognised under a law of a State or Territory dealing with the resolution of industrial disputes; or  (d) a body established or appointed, otherwise than by or under a law of a State or Territory, by:  (i) a Governor of a State; or  (ii) the Australian Capital Territory Executive; or  (iii) the Administrator of the Northern Territory; or  (iv) the Administrator of Norfolk Island; or  (v) a State or Territory Minister; or  (vi) a person holding an executive office mentioned in section 12 of the Norfolk Island Act 1979; or  (e) a person holding or performing the duties of an office established by or under, or an appointment made under, a law of a State or Territory, other than the office of head of a State or Territory Department (however described); or  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1  (f) a person holding or performing the duties of an appointment made, otherwise than under a law of a State or Territory, by:  (i) a Governor of a State; or  (ii) the Australian Capital Territory Executive; or  (iii) the Administrator of the Northern Territory; or  (iv) the Administrator of Norfolk Island; or  (v) a State or Territory Minister; or  (vi) a person holding an executive office mentioned in section 12 of the Norfolk Island Act 1979; or  (g) a State or Territory court. Making regulations to stop instrumentalities being organisations" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6C(4) Organisations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing an instrumentality of a State or Territory for the purposes of the definition of organisation in subsection (1), the Minister must:  (a) be satisfied that the State or Territory has requested that the instrumentality be prescribed for those purposes; and  (b) consider:  (i) whether treating the instrumentality as an organisation for the purposes of this Act adversely affects the government of the State or Territory; and  (ii) the desirability of regulating under this Act the collection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and transfer of personal information by the instrumentality; and  (iii) whether the law of the State or Territory regulates the collection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and transfer of personal information by the instrumentality to a standard that is at least equivalent to the standard that would otherwise apply to the instrumentality under this Act; and  (c) consult the Commissioner about the matters mentioned in subparagraphs (b)(ii) and (iii). State does not include Territory" ;
    skos:definition "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing an instrumentality of a State or Territory for the purposes of the definition of organisation in subsection (1), the Minister must:  (a) be satisfied that the State or Territory has requested that the instrumentality be prescribed for those purposes; and  (b) consider:  (i) whether treating the instrumentality as an organisation for the purposes of this Act adversely affects the government of the State or Territory; and  (ii) the desirability of regulating under this Act the collection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and transfer of personal information by the instrumentality; and  (iii) whether the law of the State or Territory regulates the collection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and transfer of personal information by the instrumentality to a standard that is at least equivalent to the standard that would otherwise apply to the instrumentality under this Act; and  (c) consult the Commissioner about the matters mentioned in subparagraphs (b)(ii) and (iii). State does not include Territory"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "23d2ef4964296581ccdfdd4d015d3e756312f6ce598f582f4dabc0d751326660" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6c ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minister must consult Commissioner before prescribing instrumentality for organisation purposes." ;
