doc:sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6C(4) Organisations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing an instrumentality of a State or Territory for the purposes of the definition of organisation in subsection (1), the Minister must:  (a) be satisfied that the State or Territory has requested that the instrumentality be prescribed for those purposes; and  (b) consider:  (i) whether treating the instrumentality as an organisation for the purposes of this Act adversely affects the government of the State or Territory; and  (ii) the desirability of regulating under this Act the collection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and transfer of personal information by the instrumentality; and  (iii) whether the law of the State or Territory regulates the collection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and transfer of personal information by the instrumentality to a standard that is at least equivalent to the standard that would otherwise apply to the instrumentality under this Act; and  (c) consult the Commissioner about the matters mentioned in subparagraphs (b)(ii) and (iii). State does not include Territory" ;
    cof:pageNumber "19"^^xsd:integer .

