doc:sch-1-sec-6d-ss-9 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6D(9) Small business and small business operators" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(9) Despite subsection (3), a body corporate is not a small business operator if it is related to a body corporate that carries on a business that is not a small business." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6DA What is the annual turnover of a business?"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-6da ;
    values:originalText "What is the annual turnover of a business for a financial year?  (1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total of the following that is earned in the year in the course of the business:  (a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;  (b) commission income;  (c) repair and service income;  (d) rent, leasing and hiring income;  (e) government bounties and subsidies;  (f) interest, royalties and dividends;  (g) other operating income. Note: The annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an entity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to the total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the Commissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the year, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments).  (2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a financial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the amount worked out using the formula: Amount that would be the annual turnover of the business under subsection (1) if the part were a whole financial year Number of days in the whole financial year Number of days in the part ×" ;
    skos:definition "What is the annual turnover of a business for a financial year?  (1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total of the following that is earned in the year in the course of the business:  (a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;  (b) commission income;  (c) repair and service income;  (d) rent, leasing and hiring income;  (e) government bounties and subsidies;  (f) interest, royalties and dividends;  (g) other operating income. Note: The annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an entity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to the total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the Commissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the year, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments).  (2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a financial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the amount worked out using the formula: Amount that would be the annual turnover of the business under subsection (1) if the part were a whole financial year Number of days in the whole financial year Number of days in the part ×"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d553881ec30ee9f45fe275f1efbd4b1a9c12606ce89e0436d4f5c05c46eec70c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-2 ;
