    cof:title "16D(6) Delayed application of National Privacy Principles to small" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) In this section: delayed application period, for an organisation, means the period:  (a) starting at the later of the following times:  (i) the start of the day when this section commences;  (ii) when the organisation became an organisation; and  (b) ending at the earlier of the following times:  (i) immediately before the first anniversary of the day when this section commences;  (ii) when the organisation carries on either a business that is not a small business or a business that involves the provision of health services." ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-16e a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16E Personal, family or household affairs"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-16e ;
    values:originalText "Nothing in the National Privacy Principles applies to:  (a) the collection, holding, use, disclosure or transfer of personal information by an individual; or  (b) personal information held by an individual; only for the purposes of, or in connection with, his or her personal, family or household affairs.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988" ;
    skos:definition "Nothing in the National Privacy Principles applies to:  (a) the collection, holding, use, disclosure or transfer of personal information by an individual; or  (b) personal information held by an individual; only for the purposes of, or in connection with, his or her personal, family or household affairs.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9b6fe2712d94c46f775b2dce1d2eff1baae14271ce70b589b3d57168816a29fd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemptions from National Privacy Principles for personal, family or household affairs" ;
