doc:sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "30(6) June each year on the operation of the code during the" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) This section does not prevent the Commissioner approving a privacy code if:  (a) the code also sets out:  (i) the period during which it will operate; or  (ii) the circumstances in which it will expire; and  (b) the Commissioner considers that the period or circumstances are appropriate." ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "30(7) June each year on the operation of the code during the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-30-2-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) This section does not prevent the Commissioner approving a privacy code if the code is expressed to apply to:  (a) all personal information or a specified type of personal information; or  (b) a specified activity or class of activities of an organisation; or  (c) a specified industry sector and/or profession; or  (d) a specified class of industry sectors and/or professions.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988  18BC  When approval takes effect" ;
    skos:definition "(7) This section does not prevent the Commissioner approving a privacy code if the code is expressed to apply to:  (a) all personal information or a specified type of personal information; or  (b) a specified activity or class of activities of an organisation; or  (c) a specified industry sector and/or profession; or  (d) a specified class of industry sectors and/or professions.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988  18BC  When approval takes effect"@en ;
