concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-68 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "68 At the end of section 27"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-68 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  (3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may, at the request of an organisation, examine the records of personal  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1  information maintained by the organisation, for the purpose of ascertaining whether the records are maintained according to:  (a) an approved privacy code that binds the organisation; or  (b) to the extent (if any) that the organisation is not bound by an approved privacy code—the National Privacy Principles." ;
    skos:definition "Add:  (3) Without limiting subsection (2), the Commissioner may, at the request of an organisation, examine the records of personal  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1  information maintained by the organisation, for the purpose of ascertaining whether the records are maintained according to:  (a) an approved privacy code that binds the organisation; or  (b) to the extent (if any) that the organisation is not bound by an approved privacy code—the National Privacy Principles."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1b7e379a57a6ee864278b9f1b4b41380bcb39f1988c7fd1fba5b1958ad9d79be" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Commissioner may examine records of an organisation upon request." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
