    values:originalText "(1C) Subsection (1A) does not prevent an individual from complaining under this Part to the Commissioner about an act done, or practice engaged in, by an organisation purportedly for the purpose of meeting (directly or indirectly) an obligation under a Commonwealth contract (whether or not the organisation is a party to the contract). Note: Section 40A requires an adjudicator for an approved privacy code to refer a code complaint to the Commissioner if the complaint is about an act or practice of a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract." ;
