    values:originalText "(2) The Commissioner may determine in writing that a specified agency to which services were or were to be provided under the contract is the respondent to the determination under section 52. The determination has effect according to its terms for the purposes of section 60. Note: This means that the amount owed by the contracted service provider will be a debt due by the agency to the complainant." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The Commissioner may determine in writing that a specified agency to which services were or were to be provided under the contract is the respondent to the determination under section 52. The determination has effect according to its terms for the purposes of section 60. Note: This means that the amount owed by the contracted service provider will be a debt due by the agency to the complainant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "efe894502342f79407965e7774ffcb7bce074e948880ca36535aaa5a75b73000" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-53b ;
