doc:sch-1-sec-55a-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "55A(5) Proceedings in the Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The court is to deal by way of a hearing de novo with the question whether the respondent has engaged in conduct that constitutes an interference with the privacy of the complainant.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988" ;
    cof:pageNumber "61"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-55a-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55A(6) Proceedings in the Federal Court or Federal Magistrates Court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-55a-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Despite subsection (5), the court may receive any of the following as evidence in proceedings about a determination made by the Commissioner under section 52:  (a) a copy of the Commissioner’s written reasons for the determination;  (b) a copy of any document that was before the Commissioner;  (c) a copy of a record (including any tape recording) of any appearance before the Commissioner (including any oral submissions made) under subsection 43(5)." ;
    skos:definition "(6) Despite subsection (5), the court may receive any of the following as evidence in proceedings about a determination made by the Commissioner under section 52:  (a) a copy of the Commissioner’s written reasons for the determination;  (b) a copy of any document that was before the Commissioner;  (c) a copy of a record (including any tape recording) of any appearance before the Commissioner (including any oral submissions made) under subsection 43(5)."@en ;
