    values:originalText "Add:  (2) Neither an adjudicator for an approved privacy code, nor a person acting under his or her direction or authority, is liable to an action, suit or proceeding in relation to an act done or omitted to be done in good faith in the exercise or purported exercise of any power or authority conferred by this Act or the code. Note: The heading to section 64 is altered by inserting “etc.” after “Commissioner”." ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-106 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "106 After subsection 66(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-106 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (1A) For the purposes of subsection (1), a journalist has a reasonable excuse if giving the information, answering the question or producing the document or record would tend to reveal the identity of a person who gave information or a document or record to the journalist in confidence." ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (1A) For the purposes of subsection (1), a journalist has a reasonable excuse if giving the information, answering the question or producing the document or record would tend to reveal the identity of a person who gave information or a document or record to the journalist in confidence."@en ;
