concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-124 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "124 Application and saving"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-124 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The amendments of section 75 of the Privacy Act 1988 made by this Schedule apply in relation to applications that are made under section 73 of that Act after the commencement of this Schedule. (2) Regulations (if any) in force for the purposes of subsection 75(3) of the Privacy Act 1988 immediately before the commencement of this Schedule have effect, after that commencement, as if they had been made for the purposes of that subsection after that commencement. (3) Subitem (2) does not prevent the amendment or repeal of the regulations." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The amendments of section 75 of the Privacy Act 1988 made by this Schedule apply in relation to applications that are made under section 73 of that Act after the commencement of this Schedule. (2) Regulations (if any) in force for the purposes of subsection 75(3) of the Privacy Act 1988 immediately before the commencement of this Schedule have effect, after that commencement, as if they had been made for the purposes of that subsection after that commencement. (3) Subitem (2) does not prevent the amendment or repeal of the regulations."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0a677fc0c24b9748a4a589dfc8dccb38d19fec4f23feafab26703862be07d520" ;
    cof:pageNumber "69"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Application and saving provisions for amendments to section 75 of the Privacy Act 1988." ;
