concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-10-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 1 An organisation must not collect sensitive information about an"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-10-2 ;
    values:originalText "individual unless:  (a) the individual has consented; or  (b) the collection is required by law; or  (c) the collection is necessary to prevent or lessen a serious and imminent threat to the life or health of any individual, where the individual whom the information concerns:  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988  (i) is physically or legally incapable of giving consent to the collection; or  (ii) physically cannot communicate consent to the collection; or  (d) if the information is collected in the course of the activities of a non-profit organisation—the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the information relates solely to the members of the organisation or to individuals who have regular contact with it in connection with its activities;  (ii) at or before the time of collecting the information, the organisation undertakes to the individual whom the information concerns that the organisation will not disclose the information without the individual’s consent; or  (e) the collection is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of a legal or equitable claim." ;
    skos:definition "individual unless:  (a) the individual has consented; or  (b) the collection is required by law; or  (c) the collection is necessary to prevent or lessen a serious and imminent threat to the life or health of any individual, where the individual whom the information concerns:  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988  (i) is physically or legally incapable of giving consent to the collection; or  (ii) physically cannot communicate consent to the collection; or  (d) if the information is collected in the course of the activities of a non-profit organisation—the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the information relates solely to the members of the organisation or to individuals who have regular contact with it in connection with its activities;  (ii) at or before the time of collecting the information, the organisation undertakes to the individual whom the information concerns that the organisation will not disclose the information without the individual’s consent; or  (e) the collection is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of a legal or equitable claim."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8f69f53fdc611497453374c19b43ee43ff06f57247c4fbc440ac9cfd6f3086ab" ;
    cof:pageNumber "85"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Organisation must not collect sensitive information about an individual unless certain conditions are met." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf> ;
