concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-2-sec-303b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "303B Acts taken to be authorised by law for purposes of Privacy Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-303b ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a disclosure or use of information by a person would be prohibited by Division 2 apart from a provision of Division 3, the disclosure or use is taken for the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, and of an approved privacy code (as defined in that Act), to be authorised by law.  (2) If a disclosure or use of information by a person would be prohibited by a provision of Division 4 apart from the fact that the disclosure or use is covered by an exception in that provision to the prohibition, the disclosure or use is taken for the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, and of an approved privacy code (as defined in that Act), to be authorised by law." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a disclosure or use of information by a person would be prohibited by Division 2 apart from a provision of Division 3, the disclosure or use is taken for the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, and of an approved privacy code (as defined in that Act), to be authorised by law.  (2) If a disclosure or use of information by a person would be prohibited by a provision of Division 4 apart from the fact that the disclosure or use is covered by an exception in that provision to the prohibition, the disclosure or use is taken for the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988, and of an approved privacy code (as defined in that Act), to be authorised by law."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c3f793ea4f4b3a4a848d2475d36c31c0d34dcfc04496d274cb9685cd3c20448e" ;
